# Week 3 Tutorial 3 Documentation

## Program Name
Student Average Calculator

## Scenario
A student has marks for three quizzes. The program asks the user to enter three quiz marks, calculates the average mark, displays the average, and determines whether the student passes or fails.

## 1. Identify the Components

### 1.1 Inputs
- Quiz 1 mark
- Quiz 2 mark
- Quiz 3 mark

### 1.2 Process
- Get three quiz marks from the user.
- Add the three quiz marks together.
- Divide the total by 3 to calculate the average.
- Check if the average is greater than or equal to 50.

### 1.3 Output
- Average mark
- Pass
- Fail
